## Quick start

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt   # or: poetry install

# 2. Configure credentials (never commit these)
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your values

# 3. Run tests
<your-framework> tests/
```

## Project structure

```
specs/          # domain specs — source of truth for what must be tested
COVERAGE.md     # aggregated coverage tracker
scripts/
  qa_track.py           # AI-usage activity tracker
  coverage_report.py    # generates coverage report from COVERAGE.md
AUTONOMY.md     # what the agent may do alone, per task, and how a task earns more
docs/decisions/ # architecture decision records (MADR)
.claude/
  settings.json # wires the hooks below
  hooks/        # protect_paths, guard_bash, stop_gate — the gates as code
  autonomy.json # current autonomy level per task, read by the hooks
  rules/        # AI agent constraints, scoped by `paths:` frontmatter
  skills/       # one folder per skill, SKILL.md inside (Agent Skills format)
```

## AI assistant setup (Claude Code)

This project is configured for [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code).

Open the project root in Claude Code — `CLAUDE.md` is loaded automatically and gives the
AI agent the full context it needs to work on tickets, write tests, and maintain coverage.
The hooks in `.claude/hooks/` need `python3` on the PATH; check them with
`python3 .claude/hooks/guard_bash.py --self-test`. The skills use the
[Agent Skills](https://agentskills.io) layout, so Codex, Cursor and Copilot can read them too.

## Adding a new test

See `CLAUDE.md` section 6 and `specs/README.md`.

